{"packet_id":"D001-01","doc_id":"D001","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley coordinated pricing algorithms ban","requirement":"A landlord may not use a coordinated pricing algorithm that uses competitor data to set or recommend rents or occupancy levels for residential units in Berkeley; selling or providing such software to Berkeley landlords is also unlawful.","key_value":"$1,000 per violation","coverage_conditions":"Residential dwelling units in the City of Berkeley; applies to landlords and to sellers or licensors of coordinated pricing algorithms.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"residential dwelling units in Berkeley"},"exemptions":"Software publishing aggregated anonymous rental data without recommending prices; products for affordable housing rent/income limits; uses for project financing market research, appraisals, or software development research/testing/training.","penalty":"Civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation, injunctive relief, damages, restitution; attorney’s fees to prevailing City Attorney or tenant.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.63","quoted_span":"It shall be unlawful for a landlord to use a coordinated pricing algorithm described
in subsection A when setting rents or occupancy levels for residential dwelling units in
the City of Berkeley. Each separate month that a violation exists or continues, and each
separate residential dwelling unit for which the landlord used the coordinated pricing
algorithm, shall constitute a separate and distinct violation.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
